  "accuracy_note": "On the test snapshot, 33.8% of eligible customers purchased again within the horizon. A rule that predicts no purchase for every customer would be right about 66.2% of the time and would have recall 0. The dummy prior model scores every customer at the training base rate. Its F1-maximizing validation threshold is 0.05, which labels every test customer as a purchaser, so its test accuracy equals the positive rate (0.338) and its recall is 1. The selected model's test accuracy was 0.698. That is a modest gap versus the 66.2% majority-class rule, which is why accuracy is a weak way to choose a model when the classes are uneven. Model choice uses validation PR-AUC.",
